/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  Missing from this case until a real control run exposed it: OpenFOAM's own
  compressible/rhoSimpleFoam/aerofoilNACA0012 tutorial, run unmodified in
  this same environment as a sanity check after the highlightInlet BC type,
  mesh quality remediation, and a ramped mass flow were each independently
  ruled out as the cause of a first-iteration pressure blowup and iteration-2
  crash, converged CLEANLY (Time=667+, residuals ~1e-7) -- proving the
  environment itself is fine and the problem was specific to this case's
  setup. The one thing present in every iteration of that working run and
  absent here: this limitTemperature fvOption, clipping T back into a
  physical range before it can propagate into the thermophysical property
  evaluation (Sutherland's law, Cp/Cv) that this case's own crash stack
  trace points at (libfluidThermophysicalModels, immediately after the
  same severe first-iteration pressure swing every attempt has shown).
  min/max reused directly from the tutorial -- a generic safety bound, not
  case-specific tuning.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      fvOptions;
}

limitT
{
    type       limitTemperature;
    min        101;
    max        1000;
    selectionMode all;
}

